note Looking at a definition without leaving the place you are reading. Hover an identifier in any code view - the document, the listing, the peek panel itself or a graph node - and what the language's server knows about it (signature, type, docs) appears as a floating tooltip; ctrl-click or double-click goes to its definition, alt-click pins the definition at the top of the right panel. The server is asked live, once per position, on a thread that stays for the session, and the answer shows a frame later. A definition inside the repo lands on the symbol, or on the line when it is inside one; one outside the repo is shown as text read from disk. A language with a grammar but no server falls back to the symbol of that name; prose files answer nothing.

